hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1084","Abu Yahya Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim Al-Bazzaz brought us strange news. I am Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Silahini. Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: “When will you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I perform the Witr prayer before I sleep, so he said to Omar: “When do you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I sleep, then pray Witr. He said: So he said to Abu Bakr: “You took it by firmness, or by a bond,” and he said to Omar: “You took it by force.” Abu Bakr said: This is according to our companions on the authority of Hammad that is mursal, but there is no Abu Qatada in it."
"1085","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Sa`id al-Darimi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad is the Meccan, Yahya ibn Sulaym, narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: “When do you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I perform the Witr prayer and then sleep. He said: “You did the Witr prayer,” and he asked Omar, and he said: “When do you perform the Witr prayer?” He said: I sleep, then get up at night and perform the Witr prayer. He said: “I should do it.” So I did.” And Muhammad bin Yahya said in the story of Omar, he said: “The strong man did, so I did.”"
"1086","Ali bin Khashram told us, Isa told us, meaning Ibn Yunus, H. Ali told us, Abdullah also told us, meaning Ibn Idris, H. Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us all, on the authority of Al-Amash, H, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, H, and Ya’qub Al-Dawraqi narrated to us. Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, they said: Al-Amash told us, H. Abu Musa told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Suleiman He is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you fears that He wakes up at the end of the night, let him perform Witr at the beginning of the night, and lie down. And whoever among you aspires to wake up at the end of the night, let him perform Witr at the end of it The late night prayer is attended, for that is better.” This is the hadith of Jesus and in the hadith of Jarir, and Abu Awanah, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
